# SYS/termcap.entry -- for the programs that will not read SYS/termcap.## gnuchess, gnuchessn and jargon all answer "'vt100': Unknown terminal type"# no matter what SYS/termcap contains -- even a minimal, correct, 127-byte# one. They share a termcap library that reads TERMCAP as the CAPABILITY# STRING ITSELF, not as the name of a file. `less' and most of the rest use a# different library that does read the file, which is why they are fine.## Source this into your shell and those programs work:##     . /dd/SYS/termcap.entry#     gnuchess## It is not set by SYS/login on purpose: TERMCAP as a PATH is what the other# 74 termcap programs on this disk expect, and that must keep working.TERMCAP='vt100|dec vt100:am:bs:co#80:li#24:cl=\E[H\E[J:cm=\E[%i%d;%dH:ce=\E[K:cd=\E[J:ho=\E[H:nd=\E[C:up=\E[A:do=\E[B:le=\b:so=\E[7m:se=\E[m:us=\E[4m:ue=\E[m:md=\E[1m:me=\E[m:ku=\EOA:kd=\EOB:kr=\EOC:kl=\EOD:'export TERMCAP